        'Find the main subject and verb first — the fragment containing them is usually (though not always) the core the rest of the sentence attaches to.',
        'Look for connector words (since, although, despite, which, that) at the start of a fragment — they signal that fragment introduces a clause and needs something specific before or after it.',
