        'When angles are given as a ratio (like 2:3:4), assign each part a variable (2x, 3x, 4x), set their sum equal to 180°, solve for x, then multiply back to get each actual angle.',
        'The exterior angle of a triangle (formed by extending one side) equals the SUM of the two interior angles that are not adjacent to it — this is faster than working out the third interior angle first and subtracting from 180°.',
