      conceptHeading: 'The approach, quickly',
      conceptBody: [
        'Check whether removing one word from a pair changes the meaning at all — if "free" adds nothing to "gift" (gifts are inherently free), the pair is redundant.',
        'Many redundant pairs involve a word that already implies time, finality, or scope: "past history" (history is already about the past), "final outcome" (an outcome is already final), "future plans" (plans are inherently about the future).',
        'A word implying "together" or "mutual" paired with another word already meaning that is a common redundancy pattern: "mutual cooperation," "join together," "combine together."',
        'The fix is almost always to simply delete the redundant word, not to replace the phrase with something else — redundancy questions test recognising the overlap, not rephrasing.',
      ],
